{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA is much stronger than image, and multiprofile avgpool with PCA improves RNA accuracy and F1 over single-profile and transformer aggregation. The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder can improve the current best RNA-only baseline. config_005 keeps the best profile/aggregation setting (multiprofile + avgpool) and only changes the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200, directly testing representation quality. This is a clean, high-value extension: if it improves, it identifies a promising RNA encoder; if not, it supports PCA as sufficient before adding more complex image or fusion changes."
}

